Package: optcompR
Title: Unified Mathematical Optimization and Computational Modeling in R
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Adam R", "Sophie", email = "adamrsophie@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: A solver independent modeling layer for mathematical
    optimization. Decision variables, parameters, expressions, constraints
    and objectives are written with ordinary R operators; models are
    classified (linear, quadratic, mixed integer, nonlinear) with recorded
    evidence, lowered to sparse standard forms, and solved by installed
    backends such as 'HiGHS' through the 'highs' package, 'OSQP',
    'NLopt', 'SCIP', and 'ROI' plugins. Results carry standardized
    termination statuses, duals with a documented sign convention,
    independent feasibility and Karush Kuhn Tucker diagnostics, exact
    derivatives, sensitivity reports and reproducibility metadata. The
    design follows 'JuMP' and 'MathOptInterface' <https://jump.dev>.
